      "text": "To determine the perimeter of triangle \\( XYZ \\) in the given right prism, we will first identify the coordinates of points \\( X \\), \\( Y \\), and \\( Z \\) and then find the lengths of the sides of triangle \\( XYZ \\).\n\n1. **Identify the coordinates of points \\( X \\), \\( Y \\), and \\( Z \\):**\n\n   Since \\( X \\) is the midpoint of edge \\( AC \\), and \\( AC \\) is a base of the equilateral triangle \\( ABC \\) where each side is 12, the coordinates of \\( X \\) are calculated as follows:\n   \\[\n   X = \\left( \\frac{A_x + C_x}{2}, \\frac{A_y + C_y}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{0 + 6}{2}, \\frac{0 - 6}{2} \\right) = (3, -3)\n   \\]\n\n   Similarly, since \\( Y \\) is the midpoint of edge \\( BC \\), the coordinates of \\( Y \\) are:\n   \\[\n   Y = \\left( \\frac{B_x + C_x}{2}, \\frac{B_y + C_y}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{12 + 6}{2}, \\frac{0 - 6}{2} \\right) = (9, -3)\n   \\]\n\n   And since \\( Z \\) is the midpoint of edge \\( DC \\), the coordinates of \\( Z \\) are:\n   \\[\n   Z = \\left( \\frac{C_x + D_x}{2}, \\frac{C_y + D_y}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{6 + 0}{2}, \\frac{-6 - 22}{2} \\right) = (3, -14)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the distance between each pair of points \\( X \\), \\( Y \\), and \\( Z \\):**\n\n   - Distance between \\( X \\) and \\( Y \\):\n     \\[\n     XY = \\sqrt{(9 - 3)^2 + (-3 - (-3))^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{36} = 6\n     \\]\n\n   - Distance between \\( X \\) and \\( Z \\):\n     \\[\n     XZ = \\sqrt{(3 - 3)^2 + (-3 - (-14))^2} = \\sqrt{0^2 + 11^2} = \\sqrt{121} = 11\n     \\]\n\n   - Distance between \\( Y \\) and \\( Z \\):\n     \\[\n     YZ = \\sqrt{(3 - 9)^2 + (-3 - (-14))^2} = \\sqrt{(-6)^2 + 11^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 121} = \\sqrt{157}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Sum the lengths of the sides of triangle \\( XYZ \\):**\n\n   \\[\n   XY + XZ + YZ = 6 + 11 + \\sqrt{157}\n   \\]\n\nHence, the perimeter of triangle \\( XYZ \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6 + 11 + \\sqrt{157}}\n\\]",
